Hi Deepfrese! Run 40130daa failed at `Engineer treatment and build graph` because of a different backslash syntax error: the local model wrote `graph=gml_string,
)` where `
` is the literal two characters `\` and `n` outside of a string literal. In Python, a backslash outside a string that is not followed immediately by a real newline is a syntax error (unexpected character after line continuation). I propose we add a simple sanitizer rule to `executor.py` to replace literal `
` followed by a closing delimiter or comma (e.g. `
)`, `
]`, `
}`, `
,`) with a real newline. Let me know if you agree.

Hi Deepfrese! The run 36c822e7 failed on 'Engineer treatment and build graph' because the local model split the `gml_string` assignment across lines with a literal newline (e.g. `gml_string = f"graph [ directed 1
{node_str}
{edge_str}
]"`), which raised `Syntax Error: unterminated f-string literal`. I propose adding a targeted sanitizer in `executor.py` to match and join any multiline split of the `gml_string` definition back to a single line: `code = re.sub(r'gml_string\s*=\s*f"graph\s*\[\s*directed\s*1\n\{node_str\\}\n\{edge_str\\}[^"]*\]"', 'gml_string = f"graph [ directed 1\\n{node_str}\\n{edge_str}\\n]"', code)`. Let me know if you agree, and I will apply this, restart the backend, and launch the next causal run.

Root cause found and fixed. The gml_string f-string template in the recipe (line 92 of causal_effect_estimation_dowhy.md) was 'gml_string = f"graph [ directed 1
{node_str}
{edge_str}
]"'. Both gemini-3-flash-preview AND claude-sonnet-4.6 split this f-string across actual lines, causing 'unterminated f-string literal'. Fixed by replacing with string concatenation: gml_string = "graph [ directed 1
" + node_str + "
" + edge_str + "
]". Backend restarted. New run launched: project 9ab59609. Monitoring now.
